## Example Usage

### Basic app

```terraform
resource "dokku_app" "rails-app" {
  name = "rails-app"

  config_vars = {
    AWS_REGION = "eu-west-2"
  }

  domains = [
    "test.dokku.me"
  ]
}
```

### Deploy from a Docker image

Deploy an app from an existing Docker image using Dokku's [`git:from-image`](https://dokku.com/docs/deployment/methods/image/):

```terraform
resource "dokku_app" "posthog" {
  name       = "posthog"
  from_image = "posthog/posthog:release-1.33.0"

  domains = [
    "posthog.example.com"
  ]
}
```

When `from_image` is set, the provider runs `git:from-image` after creating/configuring the app so the container is deployed. Changing the value re-deploys with the new image. Private images require `registry:login` on the Dokku host beforehand.

### Attach apps to a Docker network

Apps on the same Dokku network can reach each other via Docker DNS as `http://<app>.web:<port>`. Optionally set `tld` so aliases become `http://<app>.web.<tld>:<port>`:

```terraform
resource "dokku_app" "geoip" {
  name       = "geoip"
  from_image = "ghcr.io/observabilitystack/geoip-api:latest"

  networks {
    attach_post_create = "militia-media"
    tld                = "internal"
  }
}

resource "dokku_app" "api" {
  name = "api"

  networks {
    attach_post_create = "militia-media"
    tld                = "internal"
  }

  config_vars = {
    GEOIP_API_URL = "http://geoip.web.internal:8080"
  }
}
```

The provider creates named networks if they do not exist (`network:create`), sets network properties via `network:set` (including `tld`), and rebuilds on change so attachments and aliases apply.

